<title>USA: McClatchy Newspapers Q1 shr $0.40 vs $0.12.</title>
<headline>McClatchy Newspapers Q1 shr $0.40 vs $0.12.</headline>
<dateline>SACRAMENTO, Calif. 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>McCLATCHY NEWSPAPERS, INC.</p>
<p>			 SUMMARY OF UNAUDITED RESULTS</p>
<p>		    (IN THOUSANDS, EXCEPT PER SHARE AMOUNTS)</p>
<p>							    Quarter Ended</p>
<p>								 March 31</p>
<p>							  1997	   1996</p>
<p> Revenues - net				  $150,621    $146,303</p>
<p>Operating expenses:</p>
<p>	Compensation				 63,408	63,390</p>
<p>	Newsprint &amp; supplements		  21,471	31,174</p>
<p>	Depreciation and amortization	  13,250	12,996</p>
<p>	Other operating expenses		 29,702	28,646</p>
<p>	Total operating expenses		127,831     136,206</p>
<p> Operating income				  22,790	10,097</p>
<p> Interest expense				 (2,668)     (3,453)</p>
<p> Partnership (loss) income			(400)	 1,150</p>
<p> Other non-operating expenses - net	     103	    39</p>
<p> Gain on sale of newspaper operations	 6,594	    --</p>
<p> Income before taxes			     26,419	 7,833</p>
<p> Income tax provision			    11,062	 3,447</p>
<p> Net income					  15,357	 4,386</p>
<p> Net income per common share (A)		 0.40	  0.12</p>
<p> Weighted average common shares (A)	  37,984	37,616</p>
<p>(A)  Share and per share amounts have been adjusted to reflect a five-for-four stock split declared in December 1996 and paid on January 2, 1997.</p>
<p>Q197 net includes a gain of $0.10/shr on the February 1997 sale of four community newspapers. Excluding the gain and the operating results of the four newspapers from the comparisons, income in the 1997 quarter was $11.4 million or $0.30 a share, more than double the 1996 income of $4.5 million or $0.12 a share.</p>
</text>
